  "summary": "VERDICT: BLOCK\nThe default review-trace policy is bypassed for critical-risk tools unless metadata also sets `requires_review` or `mutates_state`. In `src/policy.rs:89`, trace enforcement tests only `metadata.requires_review`, while `src/policy.rs:129-130` independently makes critical-risk invocations reviewable through `critical_always_review`. Consequently, a critical, non-mutating tool with `requires_review: false` and no trace receives `review_required` instead of denial despite `require_trace_for_review: true`. The existing critical test sets both `mutates_state` and `requires_review`, so it cannot detect this path. This contradicts the documented default policy requiring trace evidence for reviewable actions and invalidates approval of policy correctness. The supplied build and clean-tree evidence otherwise supports the parent’s mechanical verification claims.",
